tramitochondrial Fe-S proteins (PubMed:18573874). The NUBP1-NUBP2 heterotetramer forms a Fe-S scaffold complex, mediating the de novo assembly of an Fe-S cluster and its transfer to target apoproteins (PubMed:18573874). Implicated in the regulation of centrosome duplication (By similarity). Negatively regulates cilium formation and structure (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}